{
 "about": "A labelled sample of law titles in the twelve UI languages, for measuring the rule topic tagger (v0.6.0 row C, Q913). The titles are hand-written in the style of national statutes; some read like real titles, and none is offered as a citation. Each item's expected topics were labelled by hand by the session that wrote them, not by a legal expert, and name the thesaurus's ENGLISH preferred label, written from memory: scripts/topic_sample_measure.py resolves each one against the operator-built thesaurus and lists every label it cannot find as unresolved, never matched loosely. Items with no expected topic test that nothing is assigned. The sample's size and choice bound what any figure measured on it means. Khmer, Lao and Burmese are not in it: their matching is tested on real words (syllable edges, every hit approximate, R690) but no figure is measured for them here.",
 "as_of": "2026-11-13",
